Easnap @PROJECT_VERSION@ | Windows x64
==================================

Screen capture, annotation, MP4 recording and GIF export for Windows 10 and 11.

START
Extract the entire ZIP to a folder you can write to. Open bin\Easnap.exe.
Easnap appears in the notification area; use its menu or press Ctrl+Shift+S
to start a capture (unless you have changed the shortcut).

Keep Easnap.exe and EasnapPreviewHost.exe together in the bin folder. The
preview helper is launched by Easnap; do not start it separately. No installer
or separate Visual C++ runtime is needed. Windows media components are required.

USE
Select a region, then take a screenshot or start an MP4/GIF recording.
Annotate screenshots, or adjust a recording's start and end in the trim window.
Use Save or Copy to publish the result. GIF export does not contain audio.

UPDATE OR REMOVE
Exit Easnap from the notification-area menu before replacing its folder.
Extract a new release into a new folder and replace both executables together.
To remove the application, exit it and delete its extracted folder.

Settings, diagnostics and temporary recordings are stored under
%LOCALAPPDATA%\Easnap, separate from this portable folder. Preserve recoverable
recordings before removing that data. Copied recording files can remain there
while the clipboard still refers to them.

RELEASE NOTES AND SUPPORT
